\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {17}{\ignorespaces The real-geometry counterpart of the toy's amplitude pile-up: activation-amplitude spectra on real Run-3 VELO event geometry, for the classical solver, the 1BQF, and the redesigned band-plus-notch response. Pink: false segments; orange: true fragments ($m\le 2$); green: findable true segments ($m\ge 3$); the dotted line is the fixed threshold. Variable track length smears the discrete toy levels into bands, and the fragment population sits inside the false bulk for every solver, the real-geometry form of the fragment floor.\relax }}{31}{figure.caption.20}\protected@file@percent }
